146j|a|A tribe of Indians allied to the Winnebagoes and Osages. They formerly inhabited the region which is now the State of Kansas, but were removed to the Indian Territory.	j:1xja,80,2~1xja,80,2
1471|n|One's acts considered as fixing one's lot in the future existence. (Theos.) The doctrine of fate as the inflexible result of cause and effect; the theory of inevitable consequence.	a:60f,48,2;vdr,38,4~vdr,38,4;60f,48,2
